    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] Yandang Mountains or Yandangshan (Chinese:  雁蕩山 ,  雁荡山 ,  \"Yàndàng Shān\",  \"Wild Goose Pond Mountain(s)\") refers, in the broad sense, to a coastal mountain range in southeastern Zhejiang province in eastern China, covering much of the prefecture-level city of Wenzhou (from Pingyang County in the south to Yueqing County in the northeast) and extending to the county-level city of Wenling in Taizhou\n[2] Yueqing () is a county-level city under the administration of Wenzhou, Zhejiang Province, in eastern China.\n[3] It is most famous for the nearby Jiayu Pass, the largest and most intact pass of the Great Wall of China.\n[4] Jiayuguan South Railway Station () is a railway station located in China's Gansu Province, Jiayuguan City."
